Vendored components (committed to this repository)
--------------------------------------------------
Unlike the test fixtures, the following third-party source IS committed to this
repository and IS distributed with it, under `vendor/`. It is vendored rather
than fetched at runtime because Basalt's modules resolve each other through
`require`, which does not work from a directory that is not on `package.path`.
See `vendor/README.md` for the provenance and how to verify it.

4. Basalt 2 (fork build) - https://github.com/HKXingluo/Basalt2
   A fork of Basalt 2 - https://github.com/Pyroxenium/Basalt2
   Copyright (c) 2025 Pyroxenium (upstream); fork maintained by HKXingluo
   Licensed under the MIT License. Full text: `vendor/LICENSE-Basalt2`.
   The fork keeps the upstream MIT licence.
   WHY THE FORK: official Basalt 2 cannot render Chinese in its text elements --
   a label or button only accepts plain text, drawn with CC's built-in font,
   which has no CJK glyphs. The fork adds `setImage()` to text elements so they
   can display a bimg bitmap. The reference project (MPlayer) is built on this
   fork, and this project follows it. The fork is a superset, so code written
   against official Basalt continues to work.
   Vendored as: `vendor/basalt.lua` — verbatim from the fork's published
   `release/basalt-full.lua` at commit
   5adef1851b1aba4cd21f566f826a7f0194a24b42 (324,622 bytes, SHA256
   5a273409fce6baaa89ae17d72332f4ad6e3c4232c3e3e426276cdbfa33a6d538).
   Used for: the entire user interface framework, including the installer's GUI.

